# Suggested ai-raccoon.ignore starter — the UNIVERSAL noise families (ADR-0086 §5: the
# ignore file is the extension surface for anything beyond the built-in deny set).
#
# Copy to <watched-root>/ai-raccoon.ignore and delete what does not apply. Every family
# below was measured as live-bank noise in at least one project on 2026-09-03; the counts
# are the evidence, not a quota — keep a line only when the path holds no real docs.
#
# Why a template and NOT a WatchDenySet extension: the deny set matches exact directory
# names at any depth for every project with no review surface. Names like `assets`,
# `snapshots` or `meta` also hold legitimate content in some repos, so promoting them
# there would silently change ingest behavior bank-wide. A copied-and-reviewed file keeps
# each project's exclusions a flagged, reviewable diff.
#
# Syntax reminder (gitignore subset, no `!` negation in v1): trailing `/` = the directory
# and everything beneath it; a pattern with no `/` at all matches at any depth; `*` stays
# within one path segment; `#` comments and blank lines are inert.

# 1. Eval corpora and golden-file fixtures — ai-raccoon leaked 788 rows across
#    tests/AiRaccoon.Tests/search_quality_eval.json (335), QueryGuard structural assets
#    (325) and scripts/retrieval_tuning/corpora/ (128). Scope per project: prefer the
#    fixture-only directory; fall back to the file when siblings must stay indexed.
# tests/<...>/search_quality_eval.json
# tests/<...>/QueryGuard/Structural/assets/
# scripts/retrieval_tuning/corpora/
**/corpora/
**/fixtures/

# 2. Snapshot / expected-output harnesses — deepseek-harness leaked 1606 rows across
#    scripts/snapshots/*/ (*.expected.json, result.json) plus a type-equiv manifest.
#    `snapshots/` and `__snapshots__/` are fixture-only by convention; keep them active.
snapshots/
__snapshots__/
*.expected.json

# 3. Generated coverage and perf reports — vue-kanban leaked 1127 rows across
#    lighthouse-report/*.report.json and coverage/coverage-final.json (+ built HTML).
#    Report directories are never project knowledge; keep these active.
coverage/
lighthouse-report/
*.report.json
coverage-final.json
TestResults/

# 4. Checklist transcripts and generated meta indexes — ai-raccoon already ignores
#    docs/work/checklist/ (large JSON command-output transcripts). The same class:
#    machine-written index/manifest JSON (jsaa docs/meta/*.json ≈ 340 rows) and
#    per-run work transcripts. Scope per project — never ignore docs/work/ wholesale;
#    jsaa holds ~10k legitimate rows under docs/work/plans+designs.
# docs/work/checklist/
# docs/meta/*.json

# 5. Vendored / mirrored duplicate trees — ai-badger indexed the same 108 KB rules.json
#    twice (skills/ and features/common/skills/, 448 rows) plus mirrored references.
#    Ignore the mirror side, never both; verify byte-identity before excluding.
# features/common/skills/
